WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:20.123
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is July eighth. Here's a tasty summer story. Japan has a special midsummer day when people eat eel to beat the heat. This year that day is coming soon, and shops have started taking reservations. Let's listen.

00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:23.675
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:24.376 --> 00:00:29.056
<v News>夏の食べ物、うなぎのニュースです。

00:00:29.756 --> 00:00:37.195
<v News>今年の夏の「土用の丑の日」は、7月26日です。

00:00:37.896 --> 00:00:43.944
<v News>日本では、この日にうなぎを食べる習慣があります。

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:51.340
<v News>これは、昔から続く、日本の夏の習慣です。

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:56.960
<v News>暑い夏を、元気に過ごすためです。

00:00:57.659 --> 00:01:03.564
<v News>うなぎには、体にいい栄養がたくさんあります。

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:11.439
<v News>今、スーパーやお店では、うなぎの予約が始まっています。

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:18.524
<v News>早いお店では、6月から予約を受け付けています。

00:01:19.224 --> 00:01:25.079
<v News>でも、うなぎの値段は、年々高くなっています。

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:33.579
<v News>国産のうなぎの蒲焼きは、1つおよそ2500円ほどします。

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:40.664
<v News>値段が高い理由は、うなぎの数が減っているからです。

00:01:41.364 --> 00:01:48.347
<v News>それでも、この日を楽しみにしている人は、たくさんいます。

00:01:49.048 --> 00:01:54.927
<v News>家で食べる人も、お店に食べに行く人もいます。

00:01:55.628 --> 00:02:01.412
<v News>お店の人は、早めの予約を勧めています。

00:02:02.111 --> 00:02:05.903
<v Host>Now let's break it down, sentence by sentence.

00:02:06.504 --> 00:02:12.984
<v Slow>日本では、この日にうなぎを食べる習慣があります。

00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:17.840
<v Host>In Japan, there is a custom of eating eel on this day.

00:02:18.439 --> 00:02:20.768
<v Vocab>習慣

00:02:21.168 --> 00:02:23.568
<v Host>It means a custom or habit.

00:02:24.168 --> 00:02:29.424
<v Slow>暑い夏を、元気に過ごすためです。

00:02:30.223 --> 00:02:33.656
<v Host>It's in order to spend the hot summer full of energy.

00:02:34.256 --> 00:02:36.704
<v Vocab>過ごす

00:02:37.104 --> 00:02:39.840
<v Host>It means to spend or pass time.

00:02:40.439 --> 00:02:46.776
<v Slow>うなぎには、体にいい栄養がたくさんあります。

00:02:47.575 --> 00:02:50.768
<v Host>Eel has lots of nutrition that is good for the body.

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:53.719
<v Vocab>栄養

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.927
<v Host>It means nutrition or nourishment.

00:02:57.527 --> 00:03:05.231
<v Slow>今、スーパーやお店では、うなぎの予約が始まっています。

00:03:06.032 --> 00:03:11.192
<v Host>Right now, at supermarkets and shops, eel reservations have begun.

00:03:11.792 --> 00:03:14.072
<v Vocab>予約

00:03:14.472 --> 00:03:17.855
<v Host>It means a reservation or booking in advance.

00:03:18.455 --> 00:03:25.295
<v Slow>早いお店では、6月から予約を受け付けています。

00:03:26.096 --> 00:03:30.463
<v Host>At the earliest shops, they have been taking reservations since June.

00:03:31.063 --> 00:03:33.584
<v Vocab>受け付ける

00:03:33.984 --> 00:03:38.111
<v Host>It means to accept or receive an application or order.

00:03:38.711 --> 00:03:45.000
<v Slow>でも、うなぎの値段は、年々高くなっています。

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.039
<v Host>But the price of eel is getting higher year by year.

00:03:49.639 --> 00:03:51.728
<v Vocab>値段

00:03:52.127 --> 00:03:54.264
<v Host>It means the price of something.

00:03:54.864 --> 00:03:57.048
<v Vocab>年々

00:03:57.448 --> 00:04:01.168
<v Host>It means year by year, little by little each year.

00:04:01.768 --> 00:04:08.608
<v Slow>値段が高い理由は、うなぎの数が減っているからです。

00:04:09.407 --> 00:04:13.728
<v Host>The reason the price is high is that the number of eels is decreasing.

00:04:14.328 --> 00:04:16.560
<v Vocab>理由

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:18.663
<v Host>It means a reason.

00:04:19.264 --> 00:04:21.232
<v Vocab>減る

00:04:21.632 --> 00:04:24.487
<v Host>It means to decrease or go down in number.

00:04:25.088 --> 00:04:32.576
<v Slow>それでも、この日を楽しみにしている人は、たくさんいます。

00:04:33.375 --> 00:04:37.432
<v Host>Even so, there are many people looking forward to this day.

00:04:38.031 --> 00:04:40.360
<v Vocab>楽しみ

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:43.879
<v Host>It means something you look forward to, a pleasure.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.480
<v Host>Let's listen to the whole story one more time.

